    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Learn a communication strategy",
    "subtitle": "How long things last · preparation 1",
    "context": "Use this subset of the reference vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U17. Discuss duration and continuing situations; extend common verb-object expressions.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U17-skill-K-HSK2-compose-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 2: compose",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "A connected everyday account keeps the same people and event status across clauses. Link the event and a reason or next action using only taught frames.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "以前",
                "pinyin": "yǐqián",
                "meaning": "before; formerly",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "23ef8698ece36f71061b7f8b95e7534ecd3e0cafd553e9b1d62dd755854aee6c"
              },
              {
                "text": "旅游",
                "pinyin": "lǚyóu",
                "meaning": "travel; go on a trip",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "249bf6122d33e3fe2101c11868ec196ec95e762e1d260d3db56a50b139dea203"
              },
              {
                "text": "没",
                "pinyin": "méi",
                "meaning": "not; have not",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "07deddfa236cc5e57b509b9f816de093af351a58380872a8556adc5b096821d8"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A friend was absent from a travel conversation. You have travelled before; the other person has not. No destination or date was given. Write an update preserving whose experience is positive and whose is negative.\nFamiliar meanings available: before; formerly; travel; go on a trip; not; have not."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
